://github.com/julianoes", "followers_url": "https://api.github.com/users/julianoes/followers", "following_url": "https://api.github.com/users/julianoes/following{/other_user}", "gists_url": "https://api.github.com/users/julianoes/gists{/gist_id}", "starred_url": "https://api.github.com/users/julianoes/starred{/owner}{/repo}", "subscriptions_url": "https://api.github.com/users/julianoes/subscriptions", "organizations_url": "https://api.github.com/users/julianoes/orgs", "repos_url": "https://api.github.com/users/julianoes/repos", "events_url": "https://api.github.com/users/julianoes/events{/privacy}", "received_events_url": "https://api.github.com/users/julianoes/received_events", "type": "User", "user_view_type": "public", "site_admin": false}, "created_at": "2024-12-19T02:57:07Z", "updated_at": "2024-12-19T02:57:23Z", "body": "Trying to reproduce this, so downloading some ulog files with PX4 v1.15.3+, on `main` branch:\r\n\r\n- Pixhawk connected via USB: :heavy_check_mark:\r\n- Pixhawk Telem1 connected via FTDI cable at 57600 baudrate: :heavy_check_mark: \r\n- Pixhawk Telem1 via SiK radio: :heavy_check_mark:\r\n- Pixhawk Telem1 via Herelink -> Tethering back to desktop: :heavy_check_mark: \r\n\r\nNow, on `v2` branch:\r\n\r\n- Pixhawk Telem1 via Herelink -> Tethering back to desktop: :heavy_check_mark: \r\n\r\nI'm wondering what version you're exactly using:\r\n\r\n> MAVSDK server version 2.1.13\r\n\r\nThis version doesn't exist. Given you're MAVSDK-Java version is 2.1.0 would mean that you're likely on server [v2.12.2](https://github.com/mavlink/MAVSDK-Java/blob/aee2c1e3f2e3fb7a4625e51be04065d1fe931a55/mavsdk_server/build.gradle#L22)\r\n\r\nThe last fix I can see would be:\r\nhttps://github.com/mavlink/MAVSDK/pull/2235\r\nwhich went into v2.5.0, so you should have that one.\r\n\r\nI'm not sure what exactly is going on to be honest :confused:.\r\n\r\nI would suggest that you try with the latest version of MAVSDK-Java which updates mavsdk_server under the hood. If it 